## The re-run asked for in review `5153400898` — posted as measured

Two runs of the exact three commands (`npm ci` → `npm run build --workspaces --if-present` → `npm run test --workspaces --if-present`, in `Blockchain/Dev`), each in a **fresh** tree (a new detached worktree with no `node_modules` and no `dist/` at the first run; `npm ci` again before the second), macOS arm64, node v24.7.0 / npm 11.5.1. `which openssl` → `/opt/homebrew/bin/openssl`, `openssl version` → **OpenSSL 3.6.3** (Homebrew's is first on `PATH`, so the LibreSSL third-workspace artefact from the doc's fifth note does not apply here — and `auth-service` reads 635/635 in both runs).

| | `cb7a3e3be` (the reviewed head, fresh tree) | `3aee3deed` (= `cb7a3e3be` + develop `8861e6216`, merged then `npm ci` again) |
|---|---|---|
| wall-clock (the test command, `date +%s` around it) | **40 s** | **58 s** |
| workspaces with a `test` script (the job's own counting script, run by hand) | **26** | **26** |
| skipped by `--if-present` | **6** — `frontend/`: admin, demo-overlay, issuer, outlook-addin, verifier, website | **6** — the same six |
| exit code | **1** | **1** |
| failing set | **2** — `anchoring-service` **1 of 172** (`threadTokenMint.test.ts › threadTokenMint emulator round-trip › parameterises mint + spend with a deterministic per-seed policyId`) · `originate` **2 of 515** (`ks444-webhooks-create-description-guard.test.ts` — `201s with a string description and stores the subscription`, `201s with description omitted`) | **1** — `anchoring-service` **1 of 208** (the same `threadTokenMint` cell) · `originate` **0 of 588** — its two `ks444` cells are green on develop `8861e6216` |

`npm ci` 22 s / build 120 s (`packages/shared/dist/index.js` absent before, present after) at `cb7a3e3be`; `npm ci` 39 s / build 115 s at the merged head. The other 24 workspaces: all green in both runs (tallies in the session record). No stack was running for either run; nothing in the set needed one.

**So it still lands on 2** at the reviewed head, with `originate`'s denominator grown from 480 to 515 since the 09-07 baseline (the same two cells fail). The doc row's stamp is updated